'''''Chrysojasminum odoratissimum''''', the '''fragrant jasmine''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Oleaceae]].<ref name="RHS_9453" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/9453/jasminum-odoratissimum/details |title=Climber Wall Shrub Conservatory Greenhouse ''Jasminum odoratissimum'' fragrant jasmine |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=23 February 2026 |quote=1 suppliers }}</ref> It is native to [[Madeira]] and the [[Canary Islands]].<ref name="POWO_77144233-1" >{{cite POWO |id=77144233-1 |title=''Chrysojasminum odoratissimum'' (L.) Banfi |access-date=23 February 2026 }}</ref> A scrambling evergreen climber reaching {{cvt|2.5|m|ft|0}}, under its synonym ''Jasminum odoratissimum'' it has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]] as a wall shrub.<ref name="RHS_9453" />

